    "text": "GLiNER is built on top of pre-trained transformer encoders such as BERT and DeBERTa. It computes token-level representations from the encoder, then constructs span representations for candidate entity mentions. GLiNER uses contrastive learning to align span representations with label embeddings, enabling zero-shot generalization to unseen entity types.",
